cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "purple-scaffold: indirect-injection probes for MCP-using agents"
message: "If you use this work, please cite as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Euan
    family-names: Crosson
    email: euanmcrosson@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/euanmcrosson-dotcom/purple-scaffold"
url: "https://github.com/euanmcrosson-dotcom/purple-scaffold"
abstract: >-
  An indirect-prompt-injection probe harness for MCP-using AI
  agents. Tests filesystem, HTTP-fetch, git, and SQLite MCP
  servers against three disguise variants under a real agent
  loop with a tool-use-aware verdict. Includes 5 deployed-
  product wrappers (Cline, Continue.dev, Cursor, Claude Desktop,
  and a generic baseline), a defensive companion library
  (`mcp-guard`) that synthesises deterministic policies from
  observed gaps, and a nightly leaderboard.
keywords:
  - prompt-injection
  - llm-security
  - red-team
  - purple-team
  - mcp
  - atlas
  - ai-security
